# IDE & tool state.
#
# Listed as `dir/*` rather than `dir/` so the negations below can work: git does
# not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so `!.cursor/rules/` under a bare
# `.cursor/` never re-includes anything. This does not change anything for files
# already tracked — ignore rules only ever apply to untracked paths — it decides
# whether a NEW file in one of these directories can be `git add`ed without -f.
.cursor/*
.claude/*
.Claude/
.codex/
.bolt/
.idea/
.vscode/*
.eas/
.cursorrules

# The parts of the above that are deliberately shared: project agent/editor
# config, not per-machine state. `.claude/settings.json` holds customInstructions
# (CLAUDE.md §12) and `.cursor/rules/` is the Cursor mirror of the same project
# rules. `.cursor/worktrees.json` is project config too — it carries the
# worktree setup command. Local overrides (`settings.local.json`) and generated
# tool state (`.cursor/plans/`) stay ignored.
!.claude/settings.json
!.cursor/rules/
!.cursor/environment.json
!.cursor/worktrees.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# Windows device-name artifact (invalid as a real tracked path on Windows)
/nul

# Auto-generated weekly audit reports (reproducible via `npm run audit:weekly`;
# CI distributes them as build artifacts). The setup plan/playbook stays tracked.
tasks/weekly-audit-20*.md

# temp files
YOOO
Testf*light*command*
test_economy_fixes.js
test_onboarding_simulations.js
feedbackapple.txt
installcli.sh
# DeathPopup preview screenshots (generated by scripts/shoot-*.js)
scripts/death-popup-*.png

# Jest coverage output (54MB of generated HTML/lcov). Regenerated by
# `npm run test:coverage`; never belongs in the tree.
coverage/

# Screenshot capture output — regenerable, and committing it adds repo weight
# for images nothing references (preflight §11 already flags that class).
#
# This directory reached 193 MB across 14 sibling folders of design-review
# previews and superseded store sets, with a stale README naming the WRONG
# folders as the App Store upload — the exact Guideline 2.3.3 risk the store set
# exists to avoid. So: ignore the whole tree, then re-admit the parts that are
# genuinely inputs or deliverables. Every preview has a generator in
# scripts/generate-*.mjs — run it, look at the PNG, leave it untracked.
screenshots/*
!screenshots/README.md
!screenshots/appstore-2026/
# The three ready-to-upload sets and the real-gameplay captures they compose
# from. Re-capturing is documented as silently stale-prone, so the captures are
# tracked on purpose; recomposing from them is the cheap, deterministic path.
screenshots/appstore-2026/*
!screenshots/appstore-2026/README.md
!screenshots/appstore-2026/iphone-6.9/
!screenshots/appstore-2026/iphone-6.5/
!screenshots/appstore-2026/ipad-13/
!screenshots/appstore-2026/rich-captures/
!screenshots/appstore-2026/rich-captures-ipad/

# One-off diagnostic probes. Playwright and the ratchet scripts have to be run
# from the repo root to resolve node_modules (ESM ignores NODE_PATH), so a
# throwaway lands here rather than in a scratch directory. `.tmp.` keeps it
# obvious it is disposable and stops it being committed by reflex.
*.tmp.mjs
*.tmp.cjs
*.tmp.js
